{%- comment -%}
ART AVENUE — MATERIAL TRUST-NOTES LIBRARY

WHAT THIS IS
------------
A standing set of pre-approved, on-brand notes that appear under the
Construction / Material buttons on a PDP when a given option is selected.
They set buyer expectations BEFORE purchase and frame natural variation as
artisanal value rather than a defect — protecting against "it didn't match
the photo" complaints while reinforcing the handmade story.

HOW IT WORKS (engine: snippets/aa-chair-config.liquid, GRID path)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
The configurator JSON carries an OPTIONAL map:

  "material_notes": {
    "<exact option value>": "<note text>",
    ...
  }

- Key MUST exactly match the Construction/Material option value (case-sensitive),
  e.g. "Kilim", "Leather", "Genuine Leather", "Solid Wood".
- The engine renders one hidden note per entry and shows only the one whose key
  matches the active material; it updates live as the buyer toggles options and
  on page load. Products without a material_notes key are unaffected.
- Styling reuses the existing helper-text look (aa-sofa__swsub) — no CSS needed.
- Notes are display-only; they are NOT pickers, variants, or line-item properties.

WRITING RULES
-------------
1. Frame variation as the value, not a disclaimer. Lead with the craft, then the
   consequence ("no two alike"), then reassurance.
2. Be specific about WHAT varies (pattern, colour, grain, tone, texture) and WHY
   (hand-cut from assorted rugs; natural hide; solid timber).
3. 1–2 sentences. Calm, confident, luxury register. No exclamation marks.
4. State plainly that the piece will differ from the photographs when true.
5. One note per material value. Don't stack multiple concerns into a wall of text.
6. Never promise uniformity you can't guarantee; never apologise.

APPROVED LIBRARY (copy these; adapt product noun only)
------------------------------------------------------
Kilim:
  "Each kilim panel is hand-cut from an assorted vintage rug, so no two pieces
   are alike. The exact pattern, colours and weave will differ from the
   photographs — that one-of-a-kind character is the essence of the piece."

Leather / Genuine Leather:
  "Made from full-grain natural leather. Subtle variation in grain, tone and
   markings is inherent to genuine hide and will develop a richer patina with
   use — each piece is unique."

Solid Wood (exposed timber):
  "Crafted from solid timber, so grain, knots and tone vary from piece to piece.
   Your item will have its own natural character and won't match the photographs
   exactly."

Marble / Stone / Travertine top:
  "Natural stone is unique — veining, colour and surface markings differ on every
   top, so your piece will not be identical to the one shown."

Handwoven / Cane / Rattan:
  "Handwoven by artisans, so minor irregularities in the weave are natural and
   expected — they are the signature of genuine handwork, not a flaw."

WHEN TO APPLY
-------------
- Kilim: ALWAYS (highest variance; assorted rug sourcing).
- Genuine leather, solid wood, natural stone, handweave: apply whenever that
  material is a selectable construction/material option, or when the material is
  fixed but variation is significant.
- Do NOT add a note for engineered/uniform materials (e.g. printed fabric,
  veneer, powder-coated metal) unless there is a real variation to disclose.

EXAMPLE (Jaisalmer Campaign Trunk — storage pilot)
--------------------------------------------------
  "material_notes": {
    "Kilim": "Each kilim panel is hand-cut from an assorted vintage rug, so no
     two pieces are alike. The exact pattern, colours and weave will differ from
     the photographs — that one-of-a-kind character is the essence of the piece."
  }

